# held/civil/axe: the hand axe (art weapon 2) at rest, hung by its head through the belt on the left hip where a sword
# would ride, so the off hand rests on it (the arms' `armed` views) (PROPS, P2b; P2c swings it and owns the culture
# forms): a bearded iron head with a lit edge over a pale ash haft. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. It serves the look's sheath
# and its held item at rest (role sheath axe, role held axe) on the sheath channel at the hip: rest, lag, sit; none where
# the clip draws it (drawn) or lays the body down (-), and none while the Chop posture's axe is in hand (prop-woodaxe).
use person
legend V linen 0
legend W linen 1
legend X linen 2
legend Y linen 3
legend Z linen 4
legend Q cloth3 0
legend R cloth3 1
legend S cloth3 2
legend T cloth3 3
legend U cloth3 4
legend I metal2 0
legend J metal2 4
body man woman
role sheath axe
role held axe
layer belt
anchor hip
keys sheath
z 30

view D key rest origin -1 3
|vv...
|vzvv.
|vyxQ.
|vxwQ.
|vv.Q.
|..QTQ
|..QSQ
|..QSQ
|..QRQ
|...Q.

